<title>USA: Security Capital Atlantic sets IPO terms.</title>
<headline>Security Capital Atlantic sets IPO terms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Security Capital Atlantic Inc set terms for its initial public offering at about $104.4 million in a regulatory filing.</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs Inc is the lead underwriter of the offering of 4.35 million shares to price in a range of $23 to $25.</p>
<p>The company has proposed to trade on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol &quot;SCA&quot;. It develops and buys multifamily properties in the southeastern United States.</p>
</text>
